    "breadcrumb": "CODAC \u003e Research thrusts",
    "content": "Leads: Dixon, Fairbanks, and Hale\nBoth learning systems that optimize objective functions and dynamical systems that obey classical mechanics can be viewed as energy-driven systems with different reactions to an energy gradient. Seeing them this way lets one set of techniques address both.\nThis thrust develops and applies new techniques for understanding composite energy-driven systems, for learning and dynamical systems alike. The work includes new approaches to online learning of optimal policies for hierarchical cyber-physical systems that mix components of learning and physics.\nPapers Journal articles and conference papers under this thrust, from the group’s Zotero library. The publications page has the center’s full list, including preprints and talks.\nCurrier, K., Leal, W., Rauta, G., Copeland, A., Dixon, W., \u0026 Fairbanks, J. P. (2026). Whitney Control Barrier Functions: A Mesh-based Geometric approach via Discrete Exterior Calculus. In IFAC. (in press). Currier, K. A., Leal, W., Fallin, B. C., Fairbanks, J. P., \u0026 Dixon, W. E. (2026). From Local to Global: Sheaf-Theoretic Control Barrier Functions on Manifolds. In IEEE Conference on Decision and Control. (to appear). Anwer, N., Riess, H., \u0026 Hale, M. (2026). Multi-Agent System Identification with Nonlinear Sheaf Diffusion. In Asilomar Conference on Signals, Systems, and Computers. (to appear). https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.11204",
