    "breadcrumb": "CODAC \u003e Research thrusts",
    "content": "Leads: Hale, Pajic, and Dixon\nDecentralized systems deployed in realistic environments have intermittent and unpredictable communications between agents, which creates challenges for the design and execution of decentralized algorithms.\nThis thrust uses cellular sheaves and homological programs to represent distributed problems, in order to systematically design algorithms that mitigate the impacts of impaired communications. Agents also often face nonconvex and mixed-integer problems, so the thrust develops new techniques that let agents jointly solve such problems even under asynchrony.\nPapers Journal articles and conference papers under this thrust, from the group’s Zotero library. The publications page has the center’s full list, including preprints and talks.\nZhao, Y., Hanks, T., Riess, H., Cohen, S., Hale, M., \u0026 Fairbanks, J. P. (2026). Asynchronous Nonlinear Sheaf Diffusion for Multi-Agent Coordination. In IEEE American Control Conference. IEEE. (accepted). https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2510.00270 Riess, H., Huang, Y., Klawonn, M., Zardini, G., \u0026 Hale, M. (2026). Quantale-Enriched Co-Design: Toward a Framework for Quantitative Heterogeneous System Design. In IEEE Conference on Decision and Control. (to appear). https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.29921 Hanks, T., Fairbanks, J. P., \u0026 Klawonn, M. (2025). Generalized Gradient Descent is a Hypergraph Functor. In Electronic Proceedings in Theoretical Computer Science (pp. 217-233). https://doi.org/10.4204/EPTCS.429.12",
