    "breadcrumb": "CODAC \u003e Research thrusts",
    "content": "Leads: Pajic, Spivak, and Hale\nMethods for modeling complex interdependencies are especially limited in dealing with different representations of uncertainty, such as stochastic versus adversarial behaviors. The two are usually handled by separate machinery that does not compose.\nThis thrust develops Moore machine-based formulations of standard modeling formalisms such as POMDPs and stochastic games. These use higher-level abstractions than existing methods, supporting the formulation of more complex stochastic and uncertain systems. On top of them, the thrust develops algorithms that exploit hierarchical structure to rapidly produce robust decision policies, even under multiple types of uncertainty.",
