    "breadcrumb": "CODAC \u003e News",
    "content": "The Air Force Office of Scientific Research, the basic research arm of the Air Force Research Laboratory, has awarded a $3.5 million University Center of Excellence for Designing Integrated, Generic, and Interoperable Compositional Analyses of Modern Systems (DIGICAMS). James Fairbanks leads the center, with co-investigators Matthew Hale, Warren Dixon, Miroslav Pajic and Kristopher Brown, and with the Topos Institute as a non-academic partner.\nThe center develops unified mathematical frameworks for the composition of decision-making processes across optimization, dynamical systems, and control, organized into five research thrusts.\nFor a plain-language account of the problem the center works on, see Drones and decisions: UF optimizing communication among autonomous units, from the University of Florida’s Herbert Wertheim College of Engineering.",
